\mt1 Zekaryah
\mt2 (Zechariah)
\is1 Introduction
\ip This document lists the prophecies of Zekaryah (Zechariah) concerning Yerushalem (Jerusalem), and tells about the hoped-for Messiah and the final judgement. It consists of two parts: \bd 1\bd*. \it Chapters 1–8\it*, Zekaryah's prophecy concerning his revelation about saving Yerushalem, the replacement of the temple and its cleaning so that Yahweh's people become holy, and \bd 2\bd*. \it Chapters 9–14\it*, the prophecies concerning the hoped-for Messiah and the final judgement.
\ip It's believed that this document was written between 520 and 518 before Yeshua/Jesus (B.C.)
\iot Main components of this document
\io1 Warnings and hope \ior 1:1–8:23\ior*
\io1 The punishment of Yisrael's enemies \ior 9:1-8\ior*
\io1 The arrival of prosperity and peace \ior 9:9–14:21\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\s1 Yisrael urged to turn to Yahweh
\rem /s1 Israel Urged to Repent; Zechariah's commission; A Call to Return to the Lord; The Lord Calls His People to Return to Him
\p
\v 1 In the eighth¦376325 month¦376324 of the second year¦376326 of \add the reign of Persian King\add* Dareyavesh¦376328 \add !(Darius¦376328)\add*, Yahweh¦376332 \add ≈spoke through\add* the prophet¦376342 Zekaryah¦376335 (\add Zechariah,\add* son of Iddo's¦376341 son Berekyah¦376338) saying¦376343,\x + \xo 1:1: \xt Ezr 4:24–5:1; 6:14.\x*
\v 2 “Yahweh¦376346 was¦376345 very angry¦376345 with your¦376349 ancestors¦376349,
\v 3 \add ≈so¦376354\add* tell \add this to\add* \add @the people\add*: Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376356 says¦376355 \add ≈that if you all turn back\add* to me¦376359, I'll¦376363 return¦376363 to you.
\v 4 Don't¦376369 be¦376371 like¦376372 your ancestors¦376372 who'd been told by the prophets¦376377 that Commander-in-chief Yahweh wanted them to¦376379 abandon \add ≈all\add* their evil practices, \add ≈but¦376388\add* they wouldn't listen¦376393 or pay¦376396 attention¦376396. That is Yahweh's¦376382 declaration¦376398.
\p
\v 5 “\add So\add* where¦376403 are¦376405 you ancestors and¦376406 the¦376406 prophets¦376406 \add now\add*? Do¦376408 they¦376405 live¦376408 forever¦376407?
\v 6 But¦376413 your¦376422 ancestors¦376422 \add ≈didn't¦376420 obey\add* my words¦376412 and my decrees that¦376414 I¦376415 commanded¦376415 \add through\add* my servants¦376418 the¦376419 prophets¦376419, but¦376410 they¦376424 \add eventually\add* repented¦376423 and said¦376424, ‘Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376427 has¦376434 done¦376434 to¦376430 us¦376430 just¦376425 what our¦376431 ways¦376431 and actions deserved.’ ”
\s1 Yahweh's compassion for Yerushalem
\rem /s1 First Vision: The Horsemen; Eight visions with their interpretations; The Man Among the Myrtle Trees; A Man among the Myrtle Trees; The Prophet's Vision of the Horses
\p
\v 7 \add ≈About three months later\add*, Yahweh¦376455 \add ≈spoke again through\add* the prophet¦376465 Zekaryah¦376458 (\add Zechariah\add* son of¦376459 Iddo's¦376464 son Berekyah¦376461) saying¦376466,
\v 8 “I \add ≈had a vision\add* in the night¦376470, and \add ≈was surprised to see¦376468\add* a man¦376473 riding¦376474 on¦376484 a red horse¦376477,\x + \xo 1:8a: \xt Rev 6:4.\x* and then he¦376479 was standing¦376480 among the myrtle¦376482 trees¦376482 that¦376483 are in the valley, and behind¦376485 him¦376485 there were¦376485 red, reddish-brown, and white¦376489 horses¦376486.”\x + \xo 1:8b: \xt Rev 6:2.\x*
\v 9 I¦376501 \add ≈asked¦376491\add*, “What¦376492 are¦376494 these¦376494 things, my¦376495 master¦376495?”
\p Then¦376491 \add ≈that\add* \add heavenly\add* messenger¦376498 who talked with¦376500 me told me, “I'll¦376502 show¦376502 you¦376502 what¦376503 those¦376494 things are.”
\p
\v 10 Then¦376508 the man¦376509 who¦376510 stood¦376510 among the myrtle¦376513 trees¦376513 answered¦376508 and¦376515 said¦376515, “Those¦376518 are¦376517 the ones that Yahweh¦376519 has¦376518 sent¦376518 out to¦376520 roam throughout the world.”
\p
\v 11 They¦376523 answered¦376523 Yahweh's¦376527 messenger¦376526 who¦376528 stood¦376528 among the myrtle¦376530 trees¦376530, telling him, “We've¦376534 been roaming throughout the world, and see, the whole¦376535 world sits \add ≈contentedly\add* and is¦376539 at peace¦376539.”
\p
\v 12 “Commander-in-chief Yahweh,” Yahweh's¦376544 messenger¦376542 \add ≈asked\add*, “how long \add ≈before\add* you show compassion¦376554 to Yerushalem¦376557 and¦376541 to the cities¦376559 of¦376559 Yehudah¦376560 \add !(Judah¦376560)\add*, which¦376561 you've¦376554 been¦376562 angry¦376562 with for the past seventy¦376564 years¦376565?”
\p
\v 13 Then¦376567 that messenger¦376571 who'd talked¦376572 with me was answered¦376567 by Yahweh¦376568 with kind and¦376567 comforting¦376577 words,
\v 14 and that messenger¦376581 told me, “Call out and say¦376585, ‘Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376588 says¦376587 this: I've been \add ≈very\add* jealous¦376590 for Yerushalem¦376591 and for Tsiyyon¦376592 \add !(Zion¦376592)\add*.
\v 15 I'm¦376598 very angry with the countries¦376602 that are at ease—I was¦376606 only a little¦376607 angry with them, \add ≈but¦376596\add* they made the disaster¦376610 worse.
\v 16 Therefore Yahweh says¦376615: I¦376617 \add ≈will show mercy\add* Yerushalem¦376618 \add ≈again\add*. My¦376620 residence will be built¦376621 within her, and¦376626 the¦376623 measuring¦376626 line will be stretched¦376628 out¦376628 over¦376629 her. That's what Commander-in-chief Yahweh declares¦376623.
\p
\v 17 “Again¦376633, call out and say¦376636, ‘Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376639 says¦376638 this: My¦376646 cities¦376643 will once again overflow¦376642 with¦376653 goodness, and \add *I\add* will again comfort¦376645 Tsiyyon¦376650 and choose¦376651 Yerushalem¦376653.’ ”
\s1 The vision of the four horns
\rem /s1 The Vision of the Horns; Four Horns and Four Blacksmiths; Four Horns and Four Craftsmen; Second Vision: The Horns and the Smiths
\p
\v 18 Then I \add ≈looked up\add* and wow, I saw four horns.
\v 19 I \add ≈asked\add* the messenger who'd talked with me, “What are those?”
\p “Those are the horns that have scattered Yehudah, Yisrael, and Yerushalem.” he \add ≈answered\add*.
\p
\v 20 Then Yahweh showed me four craftsmen
\v 21 and I \add ≈asked\add*, “What are those people coming to do?”
\p “Those horns are \add the nations\add* that scattered Yehudah so that \add ≈everyone went into hiding\add*,” he \add ≈answered\add*, “But the blacksmiths have come to terrify \add the horns\add*—to \add ≈amputate\add* the horns of the nations that \add ≈attacked\add* Yehudah, scattering \add @the people\add*.”
\c 2
\s1 The vision of Yerushalem expanded
\rem /s1 Third Vision: The Man with a Measuring Line; A Man With a Measuring Line; The Vision of the Measuring Line; Future Prosperity of Jerusalem
\p
\v 1 Then I \add ≈looked up¦376657\add*, and wow, I saw¦376661 a man \add ≈holding\add* a measuring line\f + \fr 2:1 \ft The modern equivalent would be a tape measure.\f*
\v 2 and¦376667 I¦376667 asked¦376667 him, “Where are you going?”
\p “To measure Yerushalem¦376688,” he \add ≈replied¦376667\add*, “and to¦376677 determine its width and length.”
\p
\v 3 Then¦376694 \add ≈to my surprise\add*, the messenger who'd talked with me¦376693 went away and¦376693 another messenger went out to meet him
\v 4 and told him, “Run and speak to that¦376708 young man¦376716, saying¦376699: Yerushalem \add ≈won't¦376717 need city walls\add* because \add ≈there'll be so many\add* people and animals within it¦376736.
\v 5 Yahweh declares that he'll become a wall of fire around it and will become the splendour in¦376746 the middle of it.
\s1 Yahweh commands the exiles to go home
\rem /s1 The Exiles Are Called Home; Interlude: An Appeal to the Exiles; The Exiles Are Called to Come Home
\p
\v 6 Yahweh declares: Get up \add ≈and get moving\add*. Flee from that land in the north, because I¦376751 had scattered you¦376753 into the four winds.
\v 7 \add Now\add* run you \add ≈people who¦376771 live in¦376772\add* Babylon—escape to¦376777 Tsiyyon \add !(Zion)\add*.
\v 8 Commander-in-chief Yahweh said¦376780 that, after he¦376780 honoured and¦376796 sent me against the¦376797 nations that plundered you—
\q1 because¦376794 anyone who touches you, \add ≈is messing with¦376797 God's favourite\add*.
\p
\v 9 \add He said,\add* “I¦376800 myself will \add ≈punish\add* them, and they'll be \add ≈looted by\add* their \add own\add* slaves.”
\p \add When you see that,\add* then you'll know that Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376806 sent me.
\p
\v 10 Yahweh¦376823 declares: “Sing and be glad, daughter of Tsiyyon, because¦376824 I¦376828 myself will come and settle among you¦376829.”
\p
\v 11 Then powerful nations will join Yahweh \add ≈at that time\add*, and they will become his people. He will settle among you, and you will know that Commander-in-chief Yahweh has sent me to you.
\v 12 Then Yahweh¦376848 will inherit Yehudah as his rightful possession in¦376860 that¦376856 sacred region, and will once again choose Yerushalem.
\p
\v 13 All¦376867 \add ≈people everywhere\add*, be¦376874 silent before Yahweh¦376880, because¦376866 from his sacred place, he's¦376882 been driven into action.
\c 3
\s1 Joshua and Satan
\rem /s1 Cleansing for the High Priest; Clean Garments for the High Priest; The Prophet's Vision of the High Priest; Fourth Vision: Joshua and Satan
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh showed¦376950 me¦376950 the high¦376955 priest¦376954 Yehoshua¦376953 \add !(Joshua¦376953)\add* standing in¦376957 front¦376957 of¦376958 Yahweh's¦376959 messenger¦376958, and¦376960 Satan was¦376961 standing at¦376962 his¦376964 right¦376964 to¦376965 accuse¦376965 him¦376965.\x + \xo 3:1: a \xt Ezr 5:2; \xo b \xt Rev 12:10.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈But¦376967\add* Yahweh told Satan, “May¦376972 Yahweh rebuke you, Satan—may¦376976 Yahweh who's chosen¦376979 Yerushalem¦376980, rebuke you. Isn't \add he energetic like\add* a burning¦376985 stick taken out of the fire¦376985?”\x + \xo 3:2: \xt Jude 9.\x*
\p
\v 3 Now Yehoshua was¦376988 dressed in filthy¦376991 clothes¦376989 as he¦376992 stood¦376992 in front¦376993 of¦376993 the¦376994 messenger¦376994
\v 4 \add ≈who¦377000\add* told those¦377000 standing¦377000 in front¦377002 of¦377013 him¦377002, “Take off his filthy¦377006 clothes¦377014.”
\p Then¦376996 he¦377008 said¦377008 to¦377009 Yehoshua, “Listen, I've¦377011 \add ≈taken¦377011 away¦377011 the guilt of your¦377013 disobedience\add*, and¦376996 I'll¦377014 dress you¦377015 in nice clothes.”
\p
\v 5 “Let¦377019 them¦377019 put¦377019 a clean headband on his¦377024 head,” I said¦377018, \add ≈so\add* they¦377025 placed a clean headband on Yehoshua's head and¦377018 dressed him¦377031 with \add new\add* clothes¦377031, while Yahweh's¦377034 messenger¦377033 was¦377035 standing¦377035 \add there watching\add*.
\p
\v 6 Then¦377037 \add *he¦377037\add* told Yehoshua¦377040,
\v 7 “Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦377046 says¦377045: If¦377048 you'll¦377051 \add ≈follow my instructions\add* and obey my rules, then you can govern¦377060 my \add ≈temple\add* and guard¦377065 my courtyards¦377068, because I'll¦377069 allow you to¦377070 walk¦377051 among these¦377074 who¦377073 are¦377073 standing¦377073 here.
\v 8 Please¦377078 listen, Yehoshua¦377079 the high¦377082 priest¦377081, \add ≈as well as\add* your¦377086 companions¦377084 sitting¦377085 in front¦377086 of¦377084 you¦377083. Those these men¦377089 are¦377089 a sign¦377090, because¦377087 I¦377094 myself will¦377089 bring¦377095 out my¦377098 servant¦377098 ‘the branch¦377099’.\x + \xo 3:8: \xt Jer 23:5; 33:15; Zech 6:12.\x*
\v 9 Now look at the stone that I've¦377106 placed in front¦377107 of¦377107 Yehoshua¦377108—a single¦377112 stone with seven¦377113 \add ≈faces\add* \add cut on it\add*. Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦377119 declares¦377118 that I will engrave¦377116 an inscription¦377117 on it, and¦377121 I will remove¦377121 the sin from this land¦377125 in one¦377129 day¦377128.
\v 10 Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦377134 declares¦377133 that in that day¦377131, each man¦377137 will invite¦377136 his neighbour¦377138 to¦377139 sit under his grapevine¦377142 or under his fig¦377146 tree¦377146.”\x + \xo 3:10: \xt Mic 4:4.\x*
\c 4
