\p
\v 1 Then¦377148 the¦377149 messenger¦377149 who¦377150 was¦377150 talking¦377150 with¦377151 me turned and¦377152 woke me as if waking someone from¦377157 their sleep¦377157.
\v 2 “What¦377161 do you¦377162 see¦377166?” he¦377159 \add ≈asked\add* me¦377160.
\p “Wow,” I said¦377164, “I see a lampstand¦377169 made entirely of gold¦377170, with a bowl¦377172 on top of it. It has seven lamps on the top \add ≈with a tube feeding each¦377171 one\add*,
\v 3 and¦377195 two¦377189 olive¦377190 trees¦377190 by it—one on¦377191 \add ≈each side of it\add*.”\x + \xo 4:3: \xt Rev 11:4.\x*
\v 4 Then¦377200 I¦377201 asked¦377200 the¦377204 messenger¦377204 who¦377205 was¦377205 talking¦377205 with¦377206 me¦377206, “What¦377208 are¦377210 those¦377210, my¦377211 master¦377211?”
\p
\v 5 “Don't¦377219 you¦377220 know¦377220 what those¦377224 things mean?” \add *he\add* \add ≈asked\add* me.
\p “No¦377226, my¦377227 master¦377227,” I¦377225 \add ≈replied¦377217\add*.
\p
\v 6 \add ≈So¦377229\add* he told me¦377231, “This¦377233 is¦377234 Yahweh's¦377236 message¦377234 to Zerubavel¦377239: Commander-in-chief Yahweh says¦377249 it won't¦377241 be my strength¦377242 or my power¦377244, but¦377229 with¦377242 my spirit¦377248.\x + \xo 4:6: \xt Ezr 5:2.\x*
\v 7 What are¦377255 you, big mountain¦377256? Before¦377259 Zerubavel¦377260 you will become a plain¦377261. Then he¦377262 will bring¦377262 out the¦377258 top¦377266 stone¦377265 to shouts¦377267 of ‘Grace¦377268, grace¦377269 to it¦377270.’ ”
\p
\v 8 Then Yahweh's¦377276 message¦377274 \add came\add* to¦377277 me¦377277, saying¦377278,
\v 9 “Zerubavel's¦377281 hands have laid the foundation¦377282 of¦377285 this¦377284 \add ≈temple\add* and¦377285 his¦377285 hands will bring it to completion.” Then you will \add ≈have confirmation\add* that¦377284 Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦377290 has¦377292 sent¦377292 me¦377292 to you.
\v 10 Because¦377295 who has¦377297 \add ≈mocked those¦377310 who make a small¦377299 difference\add*? They¦377300 will rejoice¦377300 and¦377301 will see¦377301 Zerubavel¦377307 \add ≈holding a plumb¦377304 line\add*.
\p Those seven¦377308 \add lamps\add* are Yahweh's¦377312 eyes¦377311 that roam over the whole¦377315 world.
\p
\v 11 “What¦377322 are¦377324 these¦377326 two¦377324 olive¦377325 trees¦377325 on the right¦377329 and¦377319 left¦377333 of¦377324 the lampstand¦377330?” I \add ≈asked\add* the messenger.\x + \xo 4:11: \xt Rev 11:4.\x*
\v 12 “And¦377337 what¦377339 are¦377341 these two olive¦377343 branches beside¦377345 the two gold¦377348 pipes¦377347 that¦377344 have golden¦377348 oil pouring¦377349 out¦377349 of them¦377350?”
\p
\v 13 Then¦377353 he¦377353 \add ≈answered¦377353\add*, “Don't¦377356 you¦377357 know¦377357 what¦377358 those¦377360 are¦377360?”
\p “No¦377362, my¦377363 master¦377363,” I¦377361 \add ≈replied¦377353\add*.
\p
\v 14 Then¦377365 he¦377365 said¦377365, “Those are¦377367 the two¦377367 \add ≈anointed¦377370 men\add*\f + \fr 4:14 \ft It's not clear who this is referring to.\f* who¦377371 stand¦377371 before the master¦377374 of the whole¦377375 world.”
\c 5
