\p
\v 1 Then¦377379 I turned around and \add ≈looked up¦377380\add*, and wow, I saw¦377382 a flying¦377385 scroll¦377384,
\v 2 and¦377392 \add @the messenger\add* \add ≈asked\add* me¦377388, “What¦377389 do you¦377390 see?”
\p “I see a flying¦377396 scroll¦377395,” I answered¦377392, “that's nine metres¦377399 long¦377397 and \add ≈half that\add* wide¦377400.”
\p
\v 3 Then¦377404 he¦377404 told me¦377405, “That's the curse¦377407 that¦377408 goes¦377408 out over¦377409 the surface¦377411 of the whole¦377412 land¦377414. Every¦377416 thief will be removed according to what it says on the one¦377424 side, and¦377404 everyone¦377416 who¦377424 \add ≈testifies falsely\add* will be removed according to what it says on the other¦377425 side.
\v 4 Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦377431 declares: I will send¦377429 it out so it will enter¦377433 into the house of \add ≈any\add* thief¦377437 and into the house of anyone¦377441 who¦377441 \add ≈testified falsely¦377443 using\add* my¦377442 name¦377442, and it will remain in¦377442 that house and \add ≈eat away at¦377442\add* its timber¦377450 and its stones¦377453.”
