\p
\v 5 Then¦377455 the¦377456 messenger¦377456 who'd been talking¦377457 with¦377458 me \add ≈came over\add* and said¦377459 to¦377460 me, “\add ≈Look up¦377461\add* and see¦377464 what's¦377465 coming now.”
\p
\v 6 “What¦377470 is¦377472 it¦377472?” I \add ≈asked¦377469\add*.
\p And¦377473 he said¦377473, “That's the measuring bin¦377475 that's coming.” Then¦377469 he \add ≈continued¦377473\add*, “That's their¦377479 eye¦377479\f + \fr 5:6 \ft Some ancient translations have ‘iniquity’ here, but we've stayed with the Hebrew.\f* across the whole¦377480 land¦377482.”
\p
\v 7 Then¦377484, wow, a lead¦377486 covering¦377485 was lifted off and¦377488 there was a woman¦377489 sitting¦377491 inside the measuring bin.
\v 8 He¦377495 said¦377495, “This¦377496 \add >woman\add* is¦377497 ‘wickedness¦377497’.” Then¦377495 he¦377498 \add ≈pushed\add* her¦377499 \add back\add* inside the measuring bin, then¦377495 \add quickly\add* pressed¦377504 the \add ≈heavy\add* lead¦377508 \add cover back\add* over its¦377511 opening.
\p
\v 9 Then I \add ≈looked up\add* \add again\add* and wow, I saw¦377516 two¦377518 women¦377519 with¦377522 wings like¦377525 stork's¦377526 wings, flying on¦377522 the wind towards us, and they¦377523 lifted¦377527 the measuring bin up \add ≈into\add* the sky.
\p
\v 10 “Where¦377542 are¦377543 they¦377543 taking¦377544 the measuring bin?” I asked¦377536 the messenger¦377539 who'd been talking¦377540 with¦377541 me.
\p
\v 11 “To build¦377551 a temple for¦377553 it in¦377555 \add ≈Babylonia\add*,” he \add ≈replied¦377549\add*. “And when it's ready, it'll¦377557 be set on a base there¦377559.”
\c 6
