\p
\v 4 My¦378981 god¦378981 Yahweh¦378980 says¦378979: “Be like a shepherd¦378982 who's watching over the flock¦378985 \add ≈that have been marked to be slaughtered¦378986\add*.
\v 5 The ones who buy¦378989 them, slaughter¦378990 them and aren't¦378991 punished, and the ones who sell¦378993 them say¦378994, ‘Blessed¦378995 be¦378995 Yahweh¦378996. I've become¦378997 rich.’ because the shepherds¦378998 working for the flocks' owners have¦379000 no pity on¦379001 them.
\p
\v 6 This is Yahweh's¦379013 declaration: I will¦379005 no longer \add ≈feel sorry for the people of this country\add*. Listen, I'm¦379015 about¦379016 to \add ≈allow everyone to be taken over\add* by \add #their neighbours¦379023\add* and by \add #their king¦379025\add* and \add allow them to\add* destroy the land¦379029, and I \add ≈won't¦379004 rescue¦379016 anyone from¦379032 them\add*.”
\p
\v 7 So¦379034 I became the shepherd of¦379037 the flock that had been marked for¦379039 slaughter¦379038—the ones who were suffering the most. I took¦379042 two¦379045 \add shepherd's\add* staffs¦379046—I named one¦379047 ‘Favour’, and the other¦379050 I named ‘Unity’, and then¦379034 I shepherded¦379053 the flock.
\v 8 Then¦379058 I destroyed the three¦379061 shepherds¦379062—in¦379063 one¦379064 month¦379063 I became impatient¦379065 with¦379063 them¦379067, and¦379058 they also¦379068 hated me¦379072.
\v 9 \add ≈So¦379074\add* I said¦379074 to the owners, “I won't¦379075 work for you¦379077 any longer as a shepherd¦379076. The sheep that are dying¦379078—let them die¦379079. The sheep that are being¦379080 destroyed—let them be¦379081 destroyed. Let¦379083 the sheep that remain \add ≈start eating each other\add*.”
