\v 10 Then¦379090 I took¦379090 my staff¦379093 \add named\add* ‘Favour’ and¦379097 broke¦379097 it¦379098 to¦379099 break¦379099 the agreement¦379102 that¦379103 I'd made¦379104 with¦379105 \add ≈all¦379107 of¦379107 my tribes\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈So¦379111\add* the agreement was broken¦379111 on that day¦379112, and the ones in the flock¦379117 who were suffering the most and who were watching¦379118 me¦379119, knew¦379114 that Yahweh¦379123 had spoken.
\v 12 Then¦379126 I told them¦379127, “If¦379128 it¦379130 seems good¦379130 to¦379127 you¦379131, \add ≈give¦379132\add* me my¦379133 wages, but¦379126 if¦379134 not¦379136, don't¦379136 \add ≈bother\add*.” So¦379126 they¦379139 \add ≈paid me thirty¦379143 silver¦379144 coins\add*.\x + \xo 11:12-13: \xt Mat 27:9-10.\x*
